      "output": "Gardner-McKenzie Damped Trend vs Linear Holt Benchmark (24-Month Horizon):\n================================================================================\nCurrent Baseline Level: $80.55M | Current Monthly Velocity: +$0.88M/month\nDamping Parameter phi : 0.88 | Asymptotic Ceiling: $87.02M\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHorizon    | Linear Forecast (Holt)   | Damped Forecast (Gardner)  | Variance Prevented\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMonth +1   | $     81.44M                | $       81.33M                | +$  0.11M Over-Forecast\nMonth +6   | $     85.84M                | $       84.02M                | +$  1.83M Over-Forecast\nMonth +12  | $     91.13M                | $       85.63M                | +$  5.51M Over-Forecast\nMonth +18  | $     96.42M                | $       86.37M                | +$ 10.05M Over-Forecast\nMonth +24  | $    101.71M                | $       86.72M                | +$ 14.99M Over-Forecast\n================================================================================\nStrategic Impact: At Month 24, linear Holt over-predicts by +$14.99M.\nVerdict: Damped trend prevents long-term capital over-commitment and facility over-building."
